+## Current bounded palette-rank audit and proposed teaching guard
+
+Outcome: **prototype**. Production generator SHA-256 remains
+`ce15c05fb1f3492ea891996c59fc224d5a42026bc65bfeffec265ced3a089ac7`,
+with canonical normalized rule hash `a51754da50c2`. No production source,
+canonical rule, approval, or admission was changed.
+
+The saved canonical two-demo lesson has a concrete finite ambiguity. Both body
+colors (3 and 8) are the numeric median of their three-color palettes. A rival
+that copies the original 5x5 seed and uses the median palette color for the
+body role only in the added area matches both complete demonstrations. On the
+saved canonical query with role colors `(5,1,9)`, it differs at `(0,7)`:
+the reference outputs 1 and the rival outputs 5. Both complete outputs, the
+exact programs, and protected Racket runtime hashes are retained below. This
+is a **saved canonical lesson** finding, not a sampled generator counterexample.
+The current `lesson_identifiable` accepts that two-demo lesson, so its palette
+variation check alone does not exclude this shortcut.
+
+The task-local `workspace/palette_rank_probe.py` supplies the reusable
+`demo_only_survivors` guard. It checks four finite extension rivals: numeric
+minimum corner role, median body role, maximum center role, and ascending
+palette roles. It uses demonstration inputs and outputs only; execution errors
+propagate rather than counting as refutations. A surviving rival requests a
+distinguishing demonstration. This remains a proposed teaching helper, not a
+production gate or a universal identifiability proof.
+
+The bounded run generated exactly 16 inputs: seeds 0 and 1, sample indices 0–7,
+default difficulty. Each sampled lesson used indices 0–2 as three demos and
+3–6 as four queries; index 7 was an additional candidate. All four rivals were
+refuted by each sampled lesson's demonstrations. No generated lesson ambiguity
+was observed within this finite scope. An already sampled input, seed 0/index
+2 with role colors `(1,5,2)`, is a concrete protected-Racket-labeled extra demo
+that refutes the median rival when appended to the two saved canonical demos.
+That candidate was selected from demo disagreement, without using query answers.
+
